Subject: [DRAFT] Pong Metal presenter: assert what it believes about the wire

Draft only. Not in any series, not built, not applied.

The presenter does not just pass the records through: it demands a reply whose
length is sizeof(PongScanoutFrame), rejects any frame whose reserved word is
non-zero, and reads format out of the same reply. Those three beliefs are
spelled out here as compile-time facts, so a wire change that breaks this
presenter breaks its build with this file named in the message.

Zero runtime change. Adopt together with pong-scanout-assert-offsets.patch.

--- a/drivers/PongMetal/PongMetalScanout.h
+++ b/drivers/PongMetal/PongMetalScanout.h
@@ -3,10 +3,24 @@
  * No readback checks, test draws, physical-address API or fabricated fence. */
 #pragma once
 #include <pthread.h>
+#include <stddef.h>
 #include <time.h>
 #include "../PongAdreno/PongScanoutWire.h"
 #include "GpuScanoutPresenter.h"
 #include "PongScanoutTiming.h"
+/* What this presenter believes about the wire, asserted here rather than only
+ * in the header it includes: the reply length it demands at the Wait call, the
+ * reserved word it refuses when non-zero, and the format it insists on. When a
+ * version changes what lives at offset 44, this is the file that must be
+ * edited on purpose, and the build says so. */
+static_assert(sizeof(PongScanoutFrame)==48 && offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,address)==8 &&
+    offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,format)==40 && offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,reserved)==44,
+    "Pong Metal presenter reply layout");
+static_assert(sizeof(PongScanoutWaitInfo)==8 && sizeof(PongScanoutDone)==16,
+    "Pong Metal presenter request and retire sizes");
+static_assert(PongScanoutVersion==1 && PongScanoutBgra==1 &&
+    PongScanoutWait==0x7002 && PongScanoutComplete==0x7003,
+    "Pong Metal presenter protocol numbers");
 namespace pongscanout {
 using Open=kern_return_t(*)(unsigned,mach_port_t,unsigned,unsigned *);
 using Call=kern_return_t(*)(unsigned,unsigned,const void *,size_t,void *,size_t *);
